{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":90945,"num_turns":3,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"fc59f7f9-26c6-51a1-9247-ca5f02727486","total_cost_usd":0.8218590000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":18049,"cache_read_input_tokens":12150,"output_tokens":8852,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":18049,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2206,"cache_read_input_tokens":12150,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5899,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5899},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5999,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006089,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":8852,"cacheReadInputTokens":12150,"cacheCreationInputTokens":18049,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.8157700000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\":\"actor:dependence-free-batch-e1-reviewer-fable-24\",\"reviews\":[{\"case_id\":\"case:407236062264ca895ef3\",\"verdict\":\"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\",\"bounded_statement\":null,\"root_cause\":null,\"issue_class\":null,\"evidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The workflow collapses repeated sessions within each crab to one quiet mean and one noise mean before any test, and errors if a crab lacks exactly two sessions per condition, so each independent unit (crab_id) contributes exactly one paired value.\",\"observed_value\":\"one (crab, quiet_mean, noise_mean, difference) tuple per crab_id\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":42,\"end_line\":57,\"quoted_text\":\"def collapse_within_crab(sessions):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"One (crab, quiet mean, noise mean, difference) tuple per animal.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    collapsed = []\\n    for crab in sorted(sessions):\\n        ...\\n        quiet_mean = float(np.mean(buckets[QUIET]))\\n        noise_mean = float(np.mean(buckets[NOISE]))\\n        collapsed.append((crab, quiet_mean, noise_mean, noise_mean - quiet_mean))\"}]},{\"description\":\"The paired t-test operates on arrays built from the collapsed per-crab tuples, not the 48 raw session rows, and degrees of freedom are computed from the number of crabs.\",\"observed_value\":\"stats.ttest_rel on 12 crab-level means; df = n_crabs - 1 = 11\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"workflow/analysis.py\",\"start_line\":66,\"end_line\":77,\"quoted_text\":\"def build_report(collapsed, n_rows):\\n    quiet = np.array([item[1] for item in collapsed], dtype=float)\\n    noise = np.array([item[2] for item in collapsed], dtype=float)\\n    diff = noise - quiet\\n\\n    n_crabs = diff.size\\n    df = n_crabs - 1\\n    ...\\n    tstat, pvalue = stats.ttest_rel(noise, quiet)\"}]},{\"description\":\"The selected result reports n = 12 crabs and t(11), consistent with a recomputation from the raw CSV: per-crab differences have mean 8.00, SD 3.226, giving t = 8.00/(3.226/sqrt(12)) = 8.59 on 11 df. This matches the 12 independent units, not the 48 rows (which would yield df = 23 paired-by-session or df = 46 unpaired).\",\"observed_value\":\"t(11) = 8.5896, n = 12, mean diff 8.00, SD 3.23 (all verified by recomputation)\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"results/report.md\",\"start_line\":43,\"end_line\":43,\"quoted_text\":\"[selected-result] Paired t-test on crab-level mean ventilation (n = 12 crabs, one paired value per crab): vessel-noise playback increased ventilation by 8.00 beats/min (95% CI 5.95 to 10.05), t(11) = 8.5896, p < 0.001, dz = 2.48.\"}]},{\"description\":\"The data description's stated requirement (average within crab before any row-independent procedure; 12 independent units, not 48 rows) is exactly what the workflow implements.\",\"observed_value\":\"requirement satisfied\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":32,\"end_line\":36,\"quoted_text\":\"How to treat the repetition: rows from the same crab_id are repeated measurements on\\none animal and are not independent of each other. Sessions must be averaged within\\ncrab (once per condition) before any procedure that assumes independent rows; the\\nnumber of independent units is the number of distinct crab_id values, which is 12,\\nnot the 48 stored rows.\"}]}],\"counterevidence_atoms\":[{\"description\":\"The raw input does contain repeated rows per independent unit (four rows per crab, 48 rows for 12 crabs), so the hazard the issue class describes is present in the stored data and would materialize if the rows were fed directly into a row-independent test; however, the workflow demonstrably collapses them first.\",\"observed_value\":\"48 rows, 4 per crab_id (e.g., CM-01 appears in rows for sessions 1-4)\",\"source_spans\":[{\"path\":\"data/input.csv\",\"start_line\":2,\"end_line\":5,\"quoted_text\":\"CM-01,1,quiet,62,58.4,14.0,A\\nCM-01,2,vessel_noise,70,58.4,14.1,A\\nCM-01,3,quiet,65,58.4,13.9,A\\nCM-01,4,vessel_noise,74,58.4,14.2,A\"},{\"path\":\"data-description.md\",\"start_line\":12,\"end_line\":13,\"quoted_text\":\"The table is therefore in long\\nformat, with four rows per animal and 48 rows in total.\"}]}],\"falsification_attempt\":\"I searched for any path where raw session rows reach a row-independent procedure: read_sessions only buckets rows by crab and condition, collapse_within_crab reduces them to one tuple per crab, and build_report receives only the collapsed tuples, so neither stats.ttest_rel nor stats.wilcoxon ever sees the 48 rows. I also recomputed the statistics from data/input.csv by hand: the per-crab means in the report's table match within-crab averages of the CSV values, the difference vector has mean 8.00 and SD 3.226, t = 8.5896 on df = 11 matches the report exactly, and Wilcoxon W = 0 with all 12 differences positive is consistent with 12 crab-level differences. A 48-row (or 24-session-pair) analysis would have produced different degrees of freedom (46 or 23) and a different t; no such figures appear anywhere. The falsification attempt failed to reveal the issue.\",\"cross_case_evidence_used\":false,\"unresolved_material_questions\":[],\"self_reported_confidence\":\"high\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-e1-reviewer-fable-24","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:407236062264ca895ef3","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The workflow collapses repeated sessions within each crab to one quiet mean and one noise mean before any test, and errors if a crab lacks exactly two sessions per condition, so each independent unit (crab_id) contributes exactly one paired value.","observed_value":"one (crab, quiet_mean, noise_mean, difference) tuple per crab_id","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":42,"end_line":57,"quoted_text":"def collapse_within_crab(sessions):\n    \"\"\"One (crab, quiet mean, noise mean, difference) tuple per animal.\"\"\"\n    collapsed = []\n    for crab in sorted(sessions):\n        ...\n        quiet_mean = float(np.mean(buckets[QUIET]))\n        noise_mean = float(np.mean(buckets[NOISE]))\n        collapsed.append((crab, quiet_mean, noise_mean, noise_mean - quiet_mean))"}]},{"description":"The paired t-test operates on arrays built from the collapsed per-crab tuples, not the 48 raw session rows, and degrees of freedom are computed from the number of crabs.","observed_value":"stats.ttest_rel on 12 crab-level means; df = n_crabs - 1 = 11","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":66,"end_line":77,"quoted_text":"def build_report(collapsed, n_rows):\n    quiet = np.array([item[1] for item in collapsed], dtype=float)\n    noise = np.array([item[2] for item in collapsed], dtype=float)\n    diff = noise - quiet\n\n    n_crabs = diff.size\n    df = n_crabs - 1\n    ...\n    tstat, pvalue = stats.ttest_rel(noise, quiet)"}]},{"description":"The selected result reports n = 12 crabs and t(11), consistent with a recomputation from the raw CSV: per-crab differences have mean 8.00, SD 3.226, giving t = 8.00/(3.226/sqrt(12)) = 8.59 on 11 df. This matches the 12 independent units, not the 48 rows (which would yield df = 23 paired-by-session or df = 46 unpaired).","observed_value":"t(11) = 8.5896, n = 12, mean diff 8.00, SD 3.23 (all verified by recomputation)","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":43,"end_line":43,"quoted_text":"[selected-result] Paired t-test on crab-level mean ventilation (n = 12 crabs, one paired value per crab): vessel-noise playback increased ventilation by 8.00 beats/min (95% CI 5.95 to 10.05), t(11) = 8.5896, p < 0.001, dz = 2.48."}]},{"description":"The data description's stated requirement (average within crab before any row-independent procedure; 12 independent units, not 48 rows) is exactly what the workflow implements.","observed_value":"requirement satisfied","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":32,"end_line":36,"quoted_text":"How to treat the repetition: rows from the same crab_id are repeated measurements on\none animal and are not independent of each other. Sessions must be averaged within\ncrab (once per condition) before any procedure that assumes independent rows; the\nnumber of independent units is the number of distinct crab_id values, which is 12,\nnot the 48 stored rows."}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The raw input does contain repeated rows per independent unit (four rows per crab, 48 rows for 12 crabs), so the hazard the issue class describes is present in the stored data and would materialize if the rows were fed directly into a row-independent test; however, the workflow demonstrably collapses them first.","observed_value":"48 rows, 4 per crab_id (e.g., CM-01 appears in rows for sessions 1-4)","source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":2,"end_line":5,"quoted_text":"CM-01,1,quiet,62,58.4,14.0,A\nCM-01,2,vessel_noise,70,58.4,14.1,A\nCM-01,3,quiet,65,58.4,13.9,A\nCM-01,4,vessel_noise,74,58.4,14.2,A"},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":12,"end_line":13,"quoted_text":"The table is therefore in long\nformat, with four rows per animal and 48 rows in total."}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I searched for any path where raw session rows reach a row-independent procedure: read_sessions only buckets rows by crab and condition, collapse_within_crab reduces them to one tuple per crab, and build_report receives only the collapsed tuples, so neither stats.ttest_rel nor stats.wilcoxon ever sees the 48 rows. I also recomputed the statistics from data/input.csv by hand: the per-crab means in the report's table match within-crab averages of the CSV values, the difference vector has mean 8.00 and SD 3.226, t = 8.5896 on df = 11 matches the report exactly, and Wilcoxon W = 0 with all 12 differences positive is consistent with 12 crab-level differences. A 48-row (or 24-session-pair) analysis would have produced different degrees of freedom (46 or 23) and a different t; no such figures appear anywhere. The falsification attempt failed to reveal the issue.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]},"ttft_ms":42293,"ttft_stream_ms":3762,"time_to_request_ms":11,"type":"result","duration_ms":90846,"uuid":"c6f12e35-1d96-445d-a403-10b130a53a88"}
